"'''Bedtime on Concordia'''" is a short story published in the developer blog for ''[[Star Wars: The Old Republic]]'' on [[October 28]], [[2014]]. It foreshadows the first appearance of [[Mandalore the Avenger|Shae Vizla]] in the ''[[Star Wars: The Old Republic: Shadow of Revan]]'' expansion, who despite being featured prominently in the promotional material for the original game, was completely absent from the game at the time of [[2011]] release. Shae appears in a story within the story, which the [[Mandalorian shock trooper|Mandalorian warrior]] [[Galron (Mandalorian)|Galron]] tells to his daughters around a campfire.

==Plot summary==
On a wide-open plain on the moon of [[Concordia/Legends|Concordia]], [[Galron (Mandalorian)|Galron]] is finishing a day of training with his young twin daughters, [[Tayn]] and [[Mari (Mandalorian)|Mari]]. He is raising them to be [[Mandalorian shock trooper|Mandalorian warriors]], just like him and [[Galron's wife|their mother]]. They have built a big fire to scare away predators and are getting ready to sleep. Mari demands a bedtime story from her father. After pretending to protest that they are getting too old for stories, Galron asks if they want to hear about the great warrior [[Mandalore the Avenger|Shae Vizla]].

It turns out that the girls have already heard most of what there is to know about Shae. They know that [[Shae Vizla's brother|her brother]] was killed by the [[Jedi Order/Legends|Jedi]], and that after that she harbored a grudge against them and preferred to fight alone. They know of her heroics during the [[Sacking of Coruscant|destruction of the Jedi Temple]]. Galron explains that she did not destroy the temple herself, but she singlehandedly breached its defenses and opened it for attack. Tayn and Mari only want to know why Shae has not fought any battles recently, especially with a [[Galactic War|new war]] raging everywhere. Their father answers that she and [[Clan Vizla|her clan]] have not been seen in years. He guesses that she is only waiting for the next challenge big enough for her.

Since the girls already know so much about Shae Vizla, Galron instead entertains them with a story of [[Mandalore the Conqueror]], even though he is fairly sure they heard it already and are only humoring him. Tayn falls asleep before he finishes, but Mari lies awake. She asks to borrow her father's helmet so that she can practice sleeping in it like a warrior. He lets her have it. Mari then, a little nervously, asks her father if he is looking for a big challenge like Shae Vizla. He assures her that she and her sister are big enough challenges for him. As Mari drifts off, Galron decides to sacrifice sleep to carve his daughters new wooden practice swords before the morning.

